WEBVTT

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.130
Oh, Yuuta. You reek of poverty again.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.590
I'm curious.

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.640
Does your whole presence radiate poverty
in proportion to lack of decent food?

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.720
I don't care for poor people.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.180
<i>Oh, she stumbled over the word.</i>

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.060
What?

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.190
Oh, nothing.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.610
Something strange is happening
with Kamakura.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:31.320
But what does it mean?

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.150
An omen of a natural disaster?

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.030
- Higashida!
- Yes?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.660
Go out with me.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.200
What's wrong?

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.450
Nothing.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.580
I just thought maybe the end
of the world is nigh.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:21.890
FUNNY STORY

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:17.970
Miyakoshi...

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:21.640
Has something happened to your brain
after ingesting your own chocolate?

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.430
No, no.

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:27.770
I just regret making you
eat that stuff every time.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.020
<i>Does she really regret it?</i>

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:36.240
And that old man said if we have love,
my cooking will get better, right?

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.030
<i>If love blossoms between you two,</i>

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.490
<i>her cooking will probably
become delicious.</i>

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.120
<i>Love her with all your heart!</i>

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.910
In short, if we go out,
I'll get good at cooking, right?

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.290
You'll feel safer that way too, Higashida.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:52.170
There's no other choice,
so let's start dating!

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.260
I love you, darling!

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:57.420
I don't know where to start.

00:02:57.670 --> 00:02:59.050
Don't call me "darling"!

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.180
Come on, it even said
in that child-rearing manual

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.520
that milk should be at body
temperature. Can't you even read?

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.310
What, you call this baby food?

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.270
Not every food should be soft.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.480
When it comes to eating,
put yourself in my place.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:18.820
And I want new clothes!

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:22.660
Only buying inexpensive items because
I'm going to get big soon is ridiculous.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.200
New and perfectly fitting items!
That's a cardinal rule!

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:26.750
Knock it off.

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:31.040
For someone who's off her game,
you're acting the same as usual.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.590
It's all Yuuta's fault!

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:40.470
I think Hime is going to fall asleep.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.220
I'll get a blanket.

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:43.720
Watch her.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:46.640
Pick you up?

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.770
<i>She gave me an order.</i>

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:51.060
<i>Well, she is a baby.</i>

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.480
SOMETHING'S LACKING

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.110
Thanks.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:06.830
SATISFIED

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:10.000
Oh. I guess her mother is best.

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:16.420
Well, I don't blame you for being anxious
about dating me, Higashida.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:18.590
It's not anxiety. I just don't want to.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.720
After all, I'm sure you've never
had a girlfriend before.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.050
And I've never had a boyfriend!

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.470
I swear I'll sew your mouth shut!

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.560
I hate studying, but I gotta do it.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.680
Let's learn
how we're supposed to go out.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:32.310
I'll bring a teacher over.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:34.150
Teacher?

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.110
Why you of all people?

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:39.730
What's this about?

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.490
Actually, we've decided to start dating.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.200
No, we haven't!

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:46.200
Congratulations.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:51.200
Kisaki, tell us as a teacher
how we can have a high school romance.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:53.580
I've never had a romance like that.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:56.580
Teacher...

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:59.590
All right then,
say whatever comes to mind!

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:05.590
To be honest, I don't care
what you two do with each other...

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:09.810
...but, um...

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.100
he should walk you
to work every day.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:14.940
Okay.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.150
And treat you.

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.020
Okay!

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:20.530
And take you to interesting places.

00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.990
Dating someone is great!

00:05:24.860 --> 00:05:25.950
<i>No way!</i>

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.330
With all those freebies, no wonder
everybody wants to date someone!

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.910
There's a lot more to it,
but you two can explore on your own.

00:05:34.620 --> 00:05:38.130
Higashida! Dating is awesome!

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:40.090
Let's go out!

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:42.380
Miyakoshi...

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:46.720
I'm not a fun guy,
and I don't have any money.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.510
Nor do I have any reason
to take it that far with you.

00:05:49.510 --> 00:05:51.600
Why are you so angry?

00:05:52.060 --> 00:05:55.270
Fine. I'll drop it for today.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.560
For today?

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.820
<i>Is she going to ask me out
every time I work here?</i>

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.530
<i>I'm gonna have to
go through this again and again?</i>

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.740
<i>What a pain in the butt!</i>

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.240
<i>Even when I tell her straight out,
it doesn't get through.</i>

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.580
<i>She only learns her lesson
after a painful experience.</i>

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.250
<i>Instead of understanding
from a half-assed explanation...</i>

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:16.710
<i>It'll be faster if we do go out,</i>

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.130
<i>I prove to her that our
personalities are a bad match,</i>

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:20.340
<i>and then we break up!</i>

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:24.710
Let's put our faith in a bright future
and go out, Miyakoshi.

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:26.220
Yay!

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:33.640
So Miyakoshi and I are dating now.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:41.940
<i>I-I don't understand it,
but my heart is suddenly broken.</i>

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.860
<i>So this is what it's like?</i>

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:46.190
<i>But at least now I can finally give up.</i>

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:48.610
C-Congratu—

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.700
But we're going to break up soon.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.120
You're going to break up?

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:54.040
I don't want you to get the wrong idea,

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:57.080
but we're not going out
because of mutual love.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.830
Miyakoshi kept bugging me
about going out,

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:04.380
and it felt like she'd keep hounding me
about it even if I turned her down.

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:07.420
Well, I figured she'd learn her lesson
if we tried it once.

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:13.890
So it's not as if I like Miyakoshi
or hate her.

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.310
When she gets fed up,
we'll break up on the spot.

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.350
<i>Miyakoshi will, that is.</i>

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:18.520
Higashida!

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:20.770
Higashida, what happened to you?

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.860
What? Nothing happened.

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:24.940
I'm as cool and calm as always.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:26.480
You can't be like always!

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:31.280
Miyakoshi is serious about you!
That's why she asked you out!

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:33.910
Saying she bugged you
or you don't like her

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:37.540
or you'll break up when she gets fed up
with you, that's being irresponsible!

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:41.540
You should really think
about Miyakoshi's feelings more!

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.880
<i>Naga is really sticking up for Hana-hana.</i>

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:46.920
<i>Is that for Hana-hana's sake?</i>

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:51.470
<i>Or for her own sake, since she wants
to put an end to her crush on him?</i>

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:53.640
<i>I don't know the answer myself!</i>

00:07:57.270 --> 00:07:59.180
<i>I explained that I don't
want her to think</i>

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:01.810
<i>that I'm not going out
with Miyakoshi because I like her...</i>

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:04.400
<i>but I still got another lecture
from Nagata.</i>

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:08.280
<i>Although if it seems
I'm really fond of her,</i>

00:08:08.280 --> 00:08:11.450
<i>then she'll feel responsible
for her own cooking.</i>

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:14.490
<i>She'll be desperate
to feed me delicious food.</i>

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.160
Higashida!

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:18.580
<i>I see.</i>

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:21.920
I'm hungry from working so hard,

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.580
so when you walk me home later,
treat me to something!

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:25.790
<i>Or do I?</i>

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:36.680
We're dating,
and you take me to an arcade?

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:39.100
You said you wanted
to go somewhere, right, Miyakoshi?

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.480
Hey! I see something!

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:50.240
<i>If you damage this machine,
it drops a stuffed animal?</i>

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:51.900
SIDE PUNCH

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:53.660
STRAIGHT-ON PUNCH

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:55.410
ADD A SPIN

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:59.200
It's impossible to do it
with three blows!

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.200
Blows?

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:15.640
Dammit! Why can't I get
this stuffed animal?

00:09:16.090 --> 00:09:17.430
Higashida!

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:19.970
Just give up on it already.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:22.680
But it's frustrating!

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:29.480
It's easier to get it by pushing
instead of picking it up.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.280
See?

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:34.780
Here.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:38.200
Don't get it yourself, stupid!

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:47.250
By the way, Miyakoshi,
are you able to talk to Saiki now?

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:48.290
Not yet.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:50.050
Even though you're the floor chief?

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.970
Yanagiba...

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.360
Wh-What's wrong?

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:10.570
I went somewhere.

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.650
You went somewhere?
Where? Down south?

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:16.150
Not school?

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:17.490
Okinawa.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.780
Okinawa?

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:21.410
- A commodity exhibition.
- A commodity exhibition?

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:25.160
I'll give you a souvenir,
Naga of the complicated mental state.

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:27.120
Okinawan Biscuits

00:10:28.960 --> 00:10:31.590
Th-Thank you.

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.090
<i>Damn that Higashida!</i>

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:42.310
<i>This is the day
I make myself clear to Saiki!</i>

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:44.600
<i>I have to find the right opportunity.</i>

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:47.770
<i>What's he doing?</i>

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.650
Looks like we're low on napkins.

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:52.650
<i>He's an alien!</i>

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.740
Higashida, emergency!
Saiki's an alien!

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:57.990
What, Miyakoshi?

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.320
Sorry to rain on your emergency,

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:02.870
but in a broad sense,
you're an alien, too.

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.740
What?

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:06.710
Are you serious?
Higashida, are you serious?

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:07.710
I'm serious.

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:09.750
This is messed up!
It's totally messed up!

00:11:10.130 --> 00:11:12.250
It is totally messed up, Miyakoshi.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:13.340
<i>Your brain.</i>

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:18.970
You both live in the same universe,
so open up to Saiki already.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:22.720
There. It's Saiki.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:29.640
We are aliens.

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:32.650
Miyakoshi! That was Japanese just now!

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:37.940
You're behind this, Kisaki.
You had Saiki say that weird line.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:42.820
Miyakoshi should also have at least
one person here she wants to avoid.

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.620
Maybe you're right, but...

00:11:45.870 --> 00:11:48.910
Fine, when I get promoted
to a higher position than Miyakoshi,

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:51.580
I'll order her to get along with Saiki.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:54.670
That's your secret ambition?

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.260
Saiki, go.

00:11:58.510 --> 00:11:59.380
Okay!

00:11:59.380 --> 00:12:01.340
You should go too, Kisaki.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:27.950
Man, when I watch Saiki at work,
I can't believe he's 20 like us.

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:30.750
I may not actually be 20 years old.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.330
Seriously? I knew it!

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:38.460
Kisaki told me you're dating Higashida.
Is it going well?

00:12:39.510 --> 00:12:43.340
I don't have any memory
of you two ever getting along.

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:46.810
Um, we've been dating
for about two weeks.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:49.270
Even though he's got
this pained look on his face,

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:51.940
he treats me to things in the end.

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:54.310
And I don't think things
have changed much from before.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.690
We're not having any problems.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:00.190
But I've gained a little weight!

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:01.490
From eating too much.

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:03.950
Higashida has lost weight, huh?

00:13:04.450 --> 00:13:05.200
Um...

00:13:05.450 --> 00:13:08.580
At the risk of meddling...

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:10.870
He's still a high school student,

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:14.460
so it's probably hard on Higashida
if you make him pay for everything.

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:17.040
Both psychologically and financially.

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:21.210
Look at how skinny he is.

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:23.380
Oh, but he eats, too.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:24.840
My cooking!

00:13:25.640 --> 00:13:27.220
<i>Physically, as well.</i>

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:36.980
After work, we should go
to another family restaurant.

00:13:38.190 --> 00:13:39.150
Miyakoshi...

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:42.940
do you enjoy
going out with me like this?

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:44.110
I guess it's okay.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:47.700
Do you feel that your cooking,
the main reason for this, is improving?

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:48.660
Nope.

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:54.040
Would you just realize already
that there's no point in us dating?

00:13:55.210 --> 00:13:56.210
Can I order a parfait?

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.790
What are you reading?

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:03.550
Muranushi recommended
that I study by reading a book.

00:14:04.720 --> 00:14:06.800
Study? That's shoujo manga.

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:09.010
All right, Higashida!

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:10.970
Should we kiss?

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.980
Higashida!

00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:17.020
DINE AND DASH

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:25.400
What's wrong, Miyakoshi?

00:14:25.650 --> 00:14:27.110
You seem down.

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.490
Yesterday, I suggested to Higashida...

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:33.950
that we kiss, and he ran away
as fast as his legs could carry him.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.420
I don't know what to tell her.

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:42.090
<i>I didn't have any money,
so I called Mom over, and she paid,</i>

00:14:42.340 --> 00:14:44.010
<i>but she was furious with me!</i>

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.090
Miyakoshi...

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:47.590
Higashida!

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:50.800
About yesterday...

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.850
I'm sorry.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.520
I shouldn't have run away like that.

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:59.310
Damn right you shouldn't have!
You left me there!

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:02.400
Do you have any idea
how nervous I was being left alone?

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:05.990
I'm really sorry.

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:08.150
MONEY FOR YESTERDAY

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:08.150
You're an idiot, Higashida!

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:09.950
<i>A chill just ran down my spine.</i>

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:14.080
Forget about what happened yesterday.
I'll make it up to you.

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:15.080
All right!

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.290
Here! I finally finished
this chocolate yesterday!

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:22.420
The wrapping is so beautiful!

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:23.420
See you!

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:24.710
Higashida!

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:28.800
It isn't going so well.

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.850
I don't know the score,
but it seems like...

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:33.350
<i>Higashida has it rough.</i>

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.980
Muranushi, a book alone isn't enough
for me to understand.

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:39.270
Show me a good example
of two people going out together.

00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:43.440
Easy for you to say.
I've never dated anyone.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:45.730
Try going out with Adachi!

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:47.610
No way!

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:52.410
Oh?

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:53.910
I mean...

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:57.790
Muranushi...

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:01.370
Miyakoshi, I not only have
no experience with dating,

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:06.090
I was rejected by someone before
expressing my feelings, so what do I know?

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:13.140
But give a little more thought
to Higashida's feelings, what he wants.

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:16.510
Otherwise...

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:18.640
he'll end up like Adachi.

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.310
I'll do it!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:24.480
<i>Oh, she's actually listening.</i>

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:26.570
You too, Muranushi!

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.820
It looks like Adachi dumped you,
but cheer up!

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:32.200
See you!

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:35.530
<i>Miyakoshi...</i>

00:16:35.950 --> 00:16:38.660
<i>That was a great slingshot suplex!</i>

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:43.920
I guess I'll get back to work.

00:16:44.380 --> 00:16:45.420
Muranushi!

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:47.170
Oh, Adachi.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:48.550
What's wrong?

00:16:49.550 --> 00:16:50.880
<i>She's not that angry?</i>

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:54.550
If you hate me so much
that you refuse to date me,

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:57.350
maybe you shouldn't
talk to me at all, right?

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:02.810
Um, look, it's just that
it suddenly came up.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:06.270
It suddenly came up,
and you let your true feeling slip.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:10.820
That goes to show you hate me
on an instinctual level.

00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:13.490
That's impressive.
Congratulations. Goodbye.

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:15.660
No, um... I like you!

00:17:18.200 --> 00:17:19.240
Uh...

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:21.250
I like you.

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:26.670
Relatively speaking... I mean.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:32.300
Relatively speaking.
How much do you like me?

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:34.880
80%? 30%? 20%?

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:39.510
SCRUNCH SCRUNCH

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.930
50%? 40%?

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:39.510
M-Muranushi...

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:43.560
Forget it.

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:45.900
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:17:46.150 --> 00:17:49.070
<i>She's back to her normal mood.</i>

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:51.820
- Sorry.
- Adachi, you really are...

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:56.160
...a fool.

00:17:59.330 --> 00:18:00.080
Muranushi!

00:18:02.540 --> 00:18:03.460
<i>No good.</i>

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:06.040
<i>She won't hear me out,
no matter what I say.</i>

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:08.080
<i>And I don't know what to say.</i>

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:11.960
<i>What should I do? I made her angry.</i>

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:14.800
<i>But if that made her mad,
then maybe...</i>

00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:16.760
<i>it's because
she feels something for me?</i>

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:18.550
<i>But even if that's not the case,</i>

00:18:18.550 --> 00:18:22.560
<i>what I blurted out earlier
made her mad or hurt her feelings</i>

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:24.480
<i>or I don't know what!</i>

00:18:30.650 --> 00:18:32.530
Long time no see, Shindou!

00:18:32.530 --> 00:18:34.240
Have you worked at the club lately?

00:18:35.150 --> 00:18:36.360
Sure I have.

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:37.820
Please come over next time.

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:42.240
Then the next time I go there,
maybe I'll buy a present for you.

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:43.450
Really?

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.580
Then make it rice! Please give me rice!

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:50.630
No, wait... Salt! I want salt!

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:54.340
SALT

00:18:57.340 --> 00:19:00.050
Wh-What should I do?

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:02.600
Don't ask me.

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.520
I'm just watching silently.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:08.270
Kisaki, Mura is an old friend of yours.

00:19:08.270 --> 00:19:10.310
Say something to Adachi.

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:11.650
Right.

00:19:11.900 --> 00:19:13.690
Adachi, I'll give you a simple,
monosyllabic word

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:19.160
that expresses both Muranushi's and
my personal feelings towards you now.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:20.950
Die.

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:22.450
Adachi!

00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:24.910
Just don't do anything hasty!

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:29.540
Adachi...

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:32.460
Higashida, do you know
where Muranushi is?

00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:34.630
She left early, a few minutes ago.

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.550
Apparently she wasn't feeling well.

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.430
R-Really?

00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:41.140
Do you happen to know
where Miyakoshi is?

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:44.510
She told me to wait in the break room,
then left, so I'm clueless.

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:45.720
Higashida...

00:19:46.640 --> 00:19:49.100
If you aren't nice to girls,

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:51.480
you'll become a scumbag like me.

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:54.980
Adachi, you're fading away!

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:56.480
Higashida!

00:19:56.690 --> 00:19:57.650
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.700
Where were you
and what were you doing, Miyakoshi?

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:04.200
Well, I had to wait until after work,
so it was a major hassle!

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:05.410
Chocolate!

00:20:07.160 --> 00:20:08.080
I bought it!

00:20:09.370 --> 00:20:11.210
What, you don't want it?

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:14.000
- It's good! I sampled it!
- Wait...

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:17.880
Why did you suddenly
buy chocolate?

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:20.970
Why? Because of
what Muranushi told me earlier.

00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:25.310
She told me to think more
about your feelings or whatever.

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:28.100
So I tried putting myself in your shoes
and thought of various things.

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:29.520
And this is the result.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.770
I thought you probably
wanted to eat something good!

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:35.980
It's just that I don't want to eat
anything that's dangerous.

00:20:35.980 --> 00:20:37.530
You're not gonna accept it?

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:38.900
Well...

00:20:39.110 --> 00:20:40.400
How can I put this?

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:43.410
<i>If you aren't nice to girls...</i>

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.910
Yes. Thank you.

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:48.040
All right!

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:50.750
Higashida accepted chocolate from me!

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:54.330
<i>She's missing the point again.
She's missing the point.</i>

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:57.300
I admire Higashida.

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:00.130
Adachi, please get a hold of yourself.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.550
Did you have an argument
with Muranushi?

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.050
An argument? About what?

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:06.050
THE CAUSE

00:21:07.390 --> 00:21:11.890
Muranushi said you should think
about the other person's feelings, Adachi!

00:21:11.890 --> 00:21:12.600
Yeah...

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:13.560
<i>I know.</i>

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:14.770
The heart!

00:21:14.770 --> 00:21:17.480
Don't give him weird advice.
Let's go home.

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:19.530
And sweets work, too!

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:27.120
<i>I don't know what's going on,</i>

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:30.580
<i>but things are getting weird
between Muranushi and Adachi.</i>

00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:32.750
Higashida!

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:37.000
It isn't just about giving chocolate.
You have to eat it, too!

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:39.000
Eat it right in front of me!

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:43.010
Okay. But I can put it in my own mouth.

00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:47.800
Well? Is it good?

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:52.850
<i>And is something funny going on
with my own sense of taste?</i>

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:56.020
Can't really taste it...

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:36.040
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:29.160
And so... Huh?
It's Higashida's raccoon dog!

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:30.570
<i>I'm a raccoon!!</i>

00:23:29.570 --> 00:23:32.030
I often see red foxes,
but raccoon dogs are rare!

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:33.240
<i>I'm not like the ones
that toady up to tourists!</i>

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:35.410
Next time, "We're All Illing."

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:36.040
WE'RE ALL ILLING
